	(text "Orange Pi CM5 board-to-board connectors JP1-JP3 (3 x Hirose DF40C-100DS-0.4V(51), 1.5 mm stack)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20.32 25.4 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.5 2.5)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "5624d389-ac11-4721-af59-1430c1ce4c1c")
	)
	(text "Pin names = Orange Pi CM5 interface PIN definition V1.1 (2025-07), IO voltage in brackets. Unused and\n\"Reserved\" pins open (JP1.64 / JP1.73: \"do not connect\"). GPIO_VREF (JP1.78) = VCC_3V3_S3, as both Orange Pi\ncarriers: GPIO1_A/B/C0/C1/C4/C6/D0-D3/D5 at 3.3 V. GPIO0 and GPIO3 are 1.8 V, GPIO4 3.3 V (base board V1.2 sheet 10)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20.32 30.48 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.5 1.5)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "de503af7-a7ee-4040-ae77-dd926da17969")
	)
	(text "System I2C (I2C4_M3 on JP1.28 / JP1.30, 3.3 V): TPS25751 I2Ct 0x20, MAX17055, BM8563 RTC 0x51"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20.32 187.96 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.5 2.5)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "caf40933-9304-49fd-b052-da2c7c789b9c")
	)
	(text "Pull-ups to VCC_3V3_S3 (bus unpowered when the CM5 is off; the PD controller and gauge run without it)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20.32 193.04 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.5 1.5)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "8b3ded3a-2a23-4946-864f-cf317afb1401")
	)
	(text "RTC + 32.768 kHz clock for the SoC (CLK32K_IN) and the Wi-Fi sleep clock (BM8563, PCF8563-compatible)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 237.49 187.96 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.5 2.5)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "ebc1504d-7bde-4516-9689-0c6a501eb391")
	)
	(text "Powered from the always-on 3.3 V. CLKOUT is open-drain (BM8563 pin table) and defaults to 32.768 kHz;\npulled up to VCC_1V8_S3 = AP6275P LPO level (1.8 V +-0.09 V, s.7) and fed to CLK32K_IN/GPIO0_B2 (JP3.96, 1.8 V)\nas on the Orange Pi base board (HYM8563 CLKOUT). INT# -> GPIO0_B0 (JP3.66) as there, pulled up to 1.8 V.\nCrystal CL 7 pF (BM8563 characterised at 8 pF)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 237.49 193.04 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.5 1.5)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "03fdd23e-4701-49fa-98c2-cd3e3f0a0f95")
	)
	(text "Buttons: power / volume on the right edge (side push, next to SD/SIM), reset / maskrom / recovery on board"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20.32 267.97 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.5 2.5)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "86a16e03-af35-4997-b1ed-97a936bc5ab6")
	)
	(text "Switch to GND, 100 Ohm series, ESD at the SoC side. PWRON_L (JP1.99) is pulled up to VBUS (45k) inside the module.\nSARADC_IN1 (JP1.68) ladder (10k pull-up to 1.8 V on the module): Recovery 0 V, Vol+ 2.2k -> 0.32 V, Vol- 6.8k -> 0.73 V."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20.32 273.05 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.5 1.5)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "ae2aaa52-d326-4fc2-ba7b-ebde21c5b0cb")
	)
	(text "Debug console (UART2_M0, 1.5 Mbaud), status LED, VSYS monitor"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 373.38 267.97 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 2.5 2.5)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "ae4e1827-6944-4e5d-9431-24b824a760e3")
	)
	(text "UART2_M0 is GPIO0_B5 / B6 = 1.8 V on the Orange Pi CM5 (JP1.55 / JP1.51): TXS0104E to 3.3 V debug pads, so a\ncommon 3.3 V USB-serial adapter can be used. VSYS_SENSE (SARADC_IN2, JP1.96) = VSYS x 499k/(1M+499k):\n4.5 V -> 1.50 V (SARADC 1.8 V full scale), 3 uA load."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 373.38 273.05 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.5 1.5)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "dd089fde-8642-4042-9167-afb7ef95d390")
	)
